%N A094350 Numbers k such that A094291(k) is not a square.
%C A094350 By the definition in A094291, it is necessary but not sufficient that x, y are chosen such that x + y <> k.
%C A094350 For these indices k, the maximum A094291(k) is reached for i = n-j-1, in the notations of that sequence (with n = k). But this can also happen for a few other k's, (k = 1, 12, 88, 609, 4180, ... =?= A081009), when i = n-j-1 gives the same value as i = n-j. A276886 appears to be a supersequence of A081009 U A094350 (this), with only very few additional terms (30, 59, 77, 106, 135, ...). - _M. F. Hasler_, Sep 02 2026
%C A094350 It appears that this sequence A094350 is a supersequence of A399306. - _Geoffrey Caveney_, Sep 03 2026
%C A094350 It appears that every term in this sequence has a minimal Lucas representation (A130310) ending either in 1, in 1010, or in 1010 followed by possibly repeated blocks 0010. Examples of the latter pattern: a(16) = 41 and A130310(41) = 10100010; a(788) = 1973 and A130310(1973) = 1010001000100010. - _Geoffrey Caveney_, Sep 03 2026
%H A094350 Hugo Pfoertner, <a href="/A094350/b094350.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..960</a>
%o A094350 (PARI) select( {is_A094350(n)=!issquare(A094291(n))}, [1..160]) \\ _M. F. Hasler_, Sep 03 2026
